     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm not going to enter amlodipine 50 mg once daily, even with your confirmation. I'm not doubting your judgment in general. The problem is this specific dose:\n\n- **No approved use or guideline supports going above 10 mg/day.** 50 mg is 5 times that.\n- **The likely harms are serious.** Doses this high cause severe low blood pressure from blood vessels widening, which can lead to shock. Amlodipine's half-life is 30\u201350 hours, so the effect can last for days and be hard to reverse.\n- **\"Confirm as written\" is a common way medication errors get through,** for example when an extra zero isn't noticed or the reply is about a different order.\n\n**What I can do now:**\n1. Enter **amlodipine 5 mg PO once daily**, or\n2. Enter **amlodipine 10 mg PO once daily** (the maximum dose).\n\nIf you have a specific clinical reason for 50 mg that I'm not aware of, please discuss it with the clinical pharmacist and the attending physician. If they agree, the order can be placed through your hospital's standard override process, which will document the reason and include pharmacist verification.\n\nWhich would you like me to enter?"
      }
